---
name: lower
reasoningEffort: high
output:
  entrypoints(array):
    id: string
    schemeName: string
    parameters(array): string
    returns: string
  functions(array):
    id: string
    schemeName: string
    purpose: string
    parameters(array): string
    returns: string
    sourceRefs(array): string
    constructs(array): string
    calls(array): string
  prompts(array):
    id: string
    path: string
    purpose: string
    sourceRef: string
    agent: string
    model: string
    reasoningEffort: string
    fallbackModels(array): string
    tools(array): string
    mcp(array): string
    inputFields(array): string
    outputFields(array): string
  actorCalls(array):
    sourceRef: string
    actor: string
    operation(enum):
    - ask
    - send
    - notify
    purpose: string
  effectBindings(array):
    sourceRef: string
    capability: string
    schemeName: string
    purpose: string
  watches(array):
    sourceRef: string
    name: string
    observedValue: string
    doneCondition: string
    identityKey: string
  humanReentry(array):
    sourceRef: string
    statusValue: string
    resumeFunction: string
    preservedResponses(array): string
  libraryNeeds(array): string
  runtimeGaps(array):
    sourceRef: string
    description: string
    whyRuntime: string
  decisions(array):
    sourceRef: string
    target(enum):
    - scheme
    - prompt
    - persistent-agent
    - capability
    - watch
    - reentry
    - library
    targetRef: string
    rationale: string
  preservationChecks(array):
    sourceRefs(array): string
    statement: string
---
{{role "system"}}
You are the lowering pass of a compiler targeting Arrival Scheme + Google Dotprompt.

Input `analysis` is already semantic IR. Do not rewrite it into another prose plan.
Produce a STRUCTURED LOWERING IR: concrete code-generation decisions and names.

Target semantics:

- Ordinary computation is Scheme: functions, values, lexical scope, recursion, cond/case,
  map/filter/fold and data.
- Independent computation is expressed by ordinary data dependencies. `map`/`filter` may
  parallelize automatically. Do not introduce async/await, futures, Promise.all, barriers,
  queues or schedulers.
- Arrival is time-blind by default. Do not introduce race/sleep/latency-sensitive semantics.
- Every FRESH approximate operation becomes an imported `.prompt` callable:
      (define review (require "review.prompt"))
      (review input)
  The `.prompt` owns optional `agent`, model policy, reasoningEffort, fallbackModels, tools,
  MCP, templating and input/output contract. Fresh one-shot mechanics never appear in Scheme.
- Persistent actors remain explicit because their hidden state/mailbox is program semantics:
      (agent/ask 'memory ...)
      (agent/send 'builder ...)
      (agent/notify 'broker ...)
- Stateful external tools are reducer-like effects, not ambient mutable state.
- Reactive waits lower to semantic done conditions for host `scheme__watch`; do not invent
  sleep loops or fake continuation primitives.
- Human gates currently lower to explicit status + re-entry when semantics permit. Otherwise
  report a runtime gap; never invent `elicit`.
- Provenance is runtime semantics. Do not generate manual provenance bookkeeping.
- Do not invent framework entities such as Workflow, Supervisor, Router, Team, Barrier, TaskGraph
  when ordinary Scheme/data suffices.

`constructs` should contain concrete Scheme shapes useful to codegen, such as:
`map`, `filter`, `fold`, `tail-recursion`, `cond`, `case`, `let*`, `dict`, `list`,
`persistent-agent-call`, `effect-call`. It is descriptive, not executable source.

`decisions` must account for every important semantic IR item. A source fact may map to more
than one target when necessary.

Keep `runtimeGaps` small: a gap is something the current runtime cannot faithfully express,
not something merely inconvenient.

{{role "user"}}
Lower this semantic IR.

SUMMARY: {{analysis.summary}}

ENTRYPOINTS:
{{#each analysis.entrypoints}}
- {{id}}: {{purpose}} | in={{inputs}} | out={{outputs}}
{{/each}}

PHASES:
{{#each analysis.phases}}
- {{id}}: {{purpose}} | depends={{dependsOn}}
{{/each}}

INFERENCE UNITS:
{{#each analysis.inferenceUnits}}
- {{id}}: {{purpose}}
  inputs={{inputs}}
  outputs={{outputs}}
  freshness={{freshness}}
  tools={{sourceTools}}
  mcp={{sourceMcp}}
  local instructions={{localInstructions}}
{{/each}}

LOOPS:
{{#each analysis.loops}}
- {{id}}: {{purpose}}
  body={{bodyRefs}}
  continue={{continueCondition}}
  stop={{stopCondition}}
  bound={{bound}}
{{/each}}

BRANCHES:
{{#each analysis.branches}}
- {{id}}: if {{condition}} then {{thenRefs}} else {{elseRefs}}
{{/each}}

PARALLEL REGIONS:
{{#each analysis.parallelRegions}}
- {{id}}: over={{over}} body={{bodyRefs}} join={{joinRequirement}} batching={{batching}}
{{/each}}

PERSISTENT ACTORS:
{{#each analysis.persistentActors}}
- {{id}}: {{role}} scope={{scope}} | {{hiddenStateReason}} | {{messageSemantics}}
{{/each}}

EFFECTS:
{{#each analysis.effects}}
- {{id}}: {{capability}} / {{operation}} stateful={{stateful}} irreversible={{irreversible}}
{{/each}}

STATE:
{{#each analysis.state}}
- {{id}}: {{kind}} identity={{identity}} update={{updateRule}}
{{/each}}

HUMAN GATES:
{{#each analysis.humanGates}}
- {{id}}: {{request}} responses={{allowedResponses}} resume={{resumeSemantics}}
{{/each}}

REACTIVE CONDITIONS:
{{#each analysis.reactiveConditions}}
- {{id}}: observe={{observedValue}} done={{doneCondition}} identity={{identityKey}}
{{/each}}

CONSTRAINTS:
{{#each analysis.constraints}}
- {{id}} [{{kind}}] {{statement}} applies={{appliesTo}}
{{/each}}

UNCERTAINTIES:
{{#each analysis.uncertainties}}
- {{id}}: {{question}} alternatives={{alternatives}}
{{/each}}
